WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.172 --> 00:00:02.755
(upbeat music)

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:06.020
- [Rebecca] Tesla on Thursday

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:09.820
released the redesigned version
of its Model S luxury sedan

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.770
dubbed the Model S Plaid.

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:13.660
(upbeat music)

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.820
(audience cheering)

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:20.080
The vehicle is priced
starting around $130,000,

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:23.200
capable of going zero to 60 miles per hour

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.690
in less than two seconds.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.560
- You know, why make this really fast car

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.190
that's crazy fast and everything.

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:34.190
And I think there is something
that's quite important

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.160
to the future of sustainable energy,

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:39.570
which is that we've got to show

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:43.465
that an electric car is
the best car, hands down.

00:00:43.465 --> 00:00:45.430
(audience applauding)

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:48.430
- [Rebecca] Model S Plaid
has a redesigned interior

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:50.500
that features three display screens.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:53.520
The vehicle has some
unusual characteristics

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.770
including a yoke shaped steering wheel.

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:59.260
- It really feels like,
okay, we're in 2021. Great.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:01.540
- [Rebecca] The idea behind
redesigns such as this one

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:04.750
typically is to drum up
renewed customer interest.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.940
Automakers have long done this.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:10.095
- So, let's deliver some cars. All right.

00:01:10.095 --> 00:01:11.497
(audience applauding)

00:01:11.497 --> 00:01:13.140
- [Rebecca] And this is just another sign

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:15.900
that Tesla in some ways has transformed

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:19.050
from a startup to an
established manufacturer.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:22.000
Chief Executive, Elon Musk said
he thought the Model S Plaid

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.280
would be in customer hands in February,

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:27.080
but found the overhaul to be
more difficult than expected

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:29.520
because of issues such
as ensuring the battery

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.890
and the revamped model is safe.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:34.700
The delay has meant that
Tesla has largely missed out

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:37.570
on what's been a booming
market for luxury vehicles

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:39.520
in the first months of this year.

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:42.390
Tesla is facing increasing
amounts of competition

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:45.080
from startups and legacy automakers alike

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.960
that are pouring money into developing

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:48.730
their own electric models.

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:51.000
The hope for Tesla is that this refresh

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.945
spurs renewed interest
in one of its classics.

00:01:53.945 --> 00:01:56.467
(bright music)

